, inflation, and policy responses."}]}, {"id": "6e92811f-1cc2-457e-ad97-d5048aab9552", "type": "topic", "title": "Consumption, Saving, Investment, and the Loanable Funds Market", "description": "Explain how saving and investment finance capital formation and connect households to long-run growth.", "children": [{"id": "ca81399d-03b1-4a9f-8f0f-4edb573ae6a2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Consumption and saving behavior", "children": [{"id": "1ac82d4d-6076-495e-bc0e-59f0b06c39c1", "type": "concept", "title": "disposable income"}, {"id": "7ec470d2-6e12-416e-8617-348760766cf9", "type": "concept", "title": "marginal propensity to consume"}, {"id": "8674128b-e180-417c-9580-50863dd30ff6", "type": "concept", "title": "marginal propensity to save"}, {"id": "c33ab2cc-7d04-4d2c-a6f7-7cd31686b3ac", "type": "concept", "title": "wealth effect"}, {"id": "d0250fb0-3f72-4c69-bd9a-5a9a7326b66b", "type": "concept", "title": "consumer expectations"}], "description": "Students learn how households allocate income between current and future spending."}, {"id": "4f2e47fc-f0b5-4b20-85ff-bc214b478f39", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Investment and capital formation", "children": [{"id": "741b48e6-743d-4704-a02a-f81756ba0877", "type": "concept", "title": "physical capital"}, {"id": "67b3fe2c-9f64-46d4-8430-2acd3f04f1d0", "type": "concept", "title": "inventory investment"}, {"id": "6943f234-fc69-447b-86e3-e04181fc4965", "type": "concept", "title": "residential investment"}, {"id": "6c2f85c9-4602-461c-83f4-9c43dc2fe960", "type": "concept", "title": "expected profitability"}, {"id": "0bb4525f-85a0-4dfb-af66-3ccaa1584991", "type": "concept", "title": "user cost of capital"}, {"id": "80eeac00-a0a8-403b-9187-ee869b134e52", "type": "concept", "title": "accelerator effect"}], "description": "This subtopic connects business investment to interest rates and expected returns."}, {"id": "d3a167e2-a05b-43a8-86fa-35e714ac734b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Loanable funds", "children": [{"id": "b45d54e7-f6