riable lags"}], "description": "Students trace how policy affects spending, output, employment, and inflation."}]}, {"id": "0efafe62-2a9b-422a-81c3-53333067de6f", "type": "topic", "title": "Fiscal Policy, Government Budgets, and Public Debt", "description": "Analyze taxes, spending, deficits, debt, multipliers, and the role of government in stabilization.", "children": [{"id": "cfe56aee-6446-4299-a330-90bd237a97f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Government spending and taxation", "children": [{"id": "ce39aca6-421c-4edd-bc30-5a7607241002", "type": "concept", "title": "transfer payments"}, {"id": "78bb9831-b69a-4420-8a7c-f7cb00ea8992", "type": "concept", "title": "government purchases"}, {"id": "2fd56597-9c01-403c-b759-fa5abf9c7afb", "type": "concept", "title": "tax revenue"}, {"id": "b67258df-1780-4faf-9ec2-43e0494847c8", "type": "concept", "title": "automatic stabilizers"}, {"id": "f954b7a1-6fc9-4636-8f19-1e3171ce6836", "type": "concept", "title": "discretionary fiscal policy"}, {"id": "21112b2e-49c1-48d1-a46f-8b49294d968b", "type": "concept", "title": "balanced budget"}], "description": "Students learn how fiscal choices affect aggregate demand and public priorities."}, {"id": "b8a744af-273e-40bf-b4d9-b79924aaf424", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multipliers and stabilization", "children": [{"id": "5b29a2e6-3d58-4395-ac47-a2c807db1ac6", "type": "concept", "title": "spending multiplier"}, {"id": "44addfb5-b1ca-4c47-bb30-75209f3063dc", "type": "concept", "title": "tax multiplier"}, {"id": "1cf0731a-2eeb-4fd7-8071-1a1ab2545e16", "type": "concept", "title": "MPC"}, {"id": "4cbeaf8f-5cd7-4d26-87e6-ee9afd0982a8", "type": "concept", "title": "fiscal stimulus"}, {"id": "953d6fb5-fbb4-41a0-ba13-72803602e78f", "type": "concept", "title": "austerity"}, {"id": "d7702703-81e4-4a93-8819-685b53cdec0c", "type": "concept", "title": "timing lag"}], "description": "This subtopic explains why fiscal policy can amplify or dampen economic fluctuations."}, {"id": "54f1c2bc-f56f-434a-9d9a-